Demographic Dividend Reality: By 2047, India’s working-age population (1.12B) will drive growth only if the dividend is harnessed within 25 years (it vanishes post-2047).
5 Non-Negotiable Guiding Principles:
Citizen prosperity > GDP growth
Open economy + private innovation
Environmental stewardship (water, land, air, forests)
Cooperative federalism (36 states/UTs)
Global implications (population + economic scale)
Critical Demographic Shifts: TFR drops to 1.8 (below replacement), life expectancy rises to 84 years, population stabilizes at 165 crore (vs. China’s 700M).
Inclusive "Developed" Definition: Achieved by 2047 only if:
Economic: $18,000/capita income
Social: 100% literacy, near-zero infant mortality
Environmental: Pristine ecosystems
Quality of life: Universal AI-enabled healthcare/education
Learning Outcomes
After engagement, learners will:

Calculate urgency: Quantify why 2024 is the starting point (12–15 years of education timeline for current youth).
Identify systemic risks: Recognize the middle-income trap (only 13% of middle-income countries escaped it in 40 years) as the top threat to 2047.
Apply 5 guiding principles: Evaluate decisions (e.g., "Will this policy advance citizen prosperity and environmental stewardship?").
Design 25-year strategies: Link short-term actions (e.g., education access, R&D funding) to 2047 outcomes (e.g., $18,000/capita, 100% literacy).
Commit to discipline: Internalize that 25+ years of unwavering focus—not short-term fixes—is the only path to avoiding the middle-income trap.
